ocked reason when a NEEDS YOU item names them (sign-off, merge, missing variable). FOUR, schema documented for all three, with the honesty rule that needs_you never invents an item: every entry cites the comment id, the stream event or the file line it came from. FIVE, tests: a fixture with one BLOCK comment, one SAFE plus CLEAN PR, one quiet seat, one failed dispatch, one PROPOSED row, and gh absent; assert the six entries and the unverified marks. VERIFY: python3 -m py_compile, tests green, desk_live.py --once against real streams of today, real exit codes. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR with Refs 73. | feat/floor-v3a

